  "rebuilt": "Optional boolean. true only for archive days rebuilt later (1–20 Oct 2026 backfill).",
  "mk_movers": "Every market entry in mk should carry g and l (up to 5 each) as [[nameAr,nameEn],'price','+x.xx%'] plus unit [ar,en] (Kuwait: فلس/fils; Saudi: ريال/SAR; UAE: درهم/AED; Qatar: ريال/QAR; Oman: ريال/OMR; Bahrain: دينار/BHD; Egypt: جنيه/EGP; US: $/$; UK: بنس/GBp). If unavailable, omit g/l and say why in note.",
  "updates": "Intraday additions go to data/updates/<date>/<HHMM>.json (encrypted), listed in index.json upd[<date>]. Add-only: never repeat items already published that day (use data/updates/<date>/seen.json, a list of sha256 hashes of normalized titles/URLs).",
  "mm": "Market-making companies (always these four, in this order): FACIL Commercial Facilities (التسهيلات التجارية), MADAR Al Madar Kuwait Holding (المدار الكويتية القابضة), THURAYA Dar Al Thuraya Real Estate (دار الثريا العقارية), TAM Tamdeen Real Estate (التمدين العقارية). Mubasher announcement pages are good for disclosures; Mubasher price snapshots have been inconsistent, so cross-check prices with Kamco, Argaam, Boursa Kuwait or newspapers.",
  "hol": "Upcoming exchange holidays within the next 60 days for the markets in the hours board.",
  "studies_dep": "Each study has dep: ops|am|wm|mm and optional a:[ar,en] 'Action for the department'. Files data/studies/<date>.json hold one or more departments; index.json studiesDep[dep] lists the dates per department. Sundays: ops (2–3), am (2–3), wm (2–3), mm (1 weekly liquidity study). Wednesdays: ops only (corporate-actions map).",
  "inf": "Conclusions layer (internal, for KMEFIC department heads and staff; never shown to clients). 4–8 items; each links today's facts into an equation, says what it means (so) and gives direct recommendations per department (rec: ops, et, am, wm, mm, mgmt). No buy/sell calls and no price forecasts. kind decides what the page computes from the day data: rights (eq: P market price fils, S subscription price fils, r new shares per existing share, rec record date, start/rtEnd/subEnd/last when known, exAlready true if P is already the ex-entitlement price, v 'exp' while dates are unconfirmed; the page computes TERP, right value, discount, loss if idle, cum = record − 3 Kuwait trading days, and draws the rights timeline), market (uses mk + tape), movers (grp: indexes into the kw g/l lists), mm (eq.series: recent closes per code), load (extra: computed deadlines [date,[ar,en]]; the page counts ev + ev2 + extra per day for 24 days), note (any other equation: keys [[label],[value],[up|down|'']] + f text). conf: high = official sources agree, med = one strong source or partly computed, low = thin evidence. chk = [review date, what will prove it right or wrong]. view.pts = 3–5 one-line headlines, each pointing to an item id. log = the conclusions log (kept in hub-assets/inf/log.json, see README): recent items with their review results (res ok/no/part, resN = what happened).",
  "ipo": "IPO radar, in its own file data/ipo/YYYY-MM-DD.json (encrypted), listed in index.json 'ipo'. The page shows the latest radar file on the latest day, and the last file on or before the day for archive days. Facts only; the page builds the options, the client Q&A and the management brief from the fields. post = IPOs KMEFIC clients took part in (post-IPO tracking for Wealth Management). Intraday updates may carry ipo.items / ipo.post (same id replaces).",
  "signal": "t: one idea, max 80 chars, plain words; s: one line, max 120; p: the explanation. Name markets ('بورصة الكويت', 'السوق السعودية', 'البورصة المصرية'), never nicknames or index codes in t/s. refs: items whose sources back every claim; a cause is written only if a source states it for that market. Check with tools/qa_check.mjs before encrypting.",
  "inf_x4": "Cross-study required before any conclusion: x4 (news, mkt, geo, str), agree, chain, kb; rec in guidance tone. See README 'Knowledge bank and cross-study'."
 },
